{
 "name": "merlthor-strait",
 "about": "The south-west of the game's own world painting The Three Great Continents at its high-resolution size (Vylbrand and Limsa Lominsa, the Strait of Merlthor, Thanalan with Vesper Bay's cape and Ul'dah, the eastern lobe, the Rhotano Sea and its compass roses, the galleon in the east), read as a chart under the moon: violet sea, the land's dark ground warmed toward rose-copper, the ferry's crossing from Vesper Bay to Limsa and the roads out of Ul'dah engraved over it in gilt, where the runtime's glints run. Crop [0, 1335, 1100, 825] (the charter's): 21.8% of its own area over 3-1's crop [0, 555, 1280, 960], 1.5% over 2-3's, none over 3-5's. The painting fades to black at its foot, so a faint violet lift over the whole board (a glow of radius 2000) keeps the dark ground off sRGB 0-1 for the converter's gate (MR 3 round 1, critic B1). The rose-copper region follows the painting's dark land (a luma ramp), fades within 75 units of the walls, below y 400-460 (the fade) and round the launcher, and leaves the Sagolii's interior (a disc 160 units across, under its two ridge crowns) to the violet so the orange crowns keep F9's separation.",
